        "subject": "LU-20844 tcu: extend fid2path APIs to resolve trash object",
        "message": "LU-20844 tcu: extend fid2path APIs to resolve trash object\n\nExtend fid2path APIs to resolve the original path and the trash path\nof an object in Trash Can. The changes include:\n- Make the MDT stop the LinkEA walk of mdt_path_current() at\n  LU_TRASH_FID and prefix the result with \".ltrash/\", so that\n  llapi_fid2path/_at() can resolve a deleted object to its trash path.\n- Append a new variable length field to struct lustre_unrm_xattr for\n  different kinds of extension, but its base header is not changed.\n- Add a new flag URM_FL_TS_APPEND and set it when a timestamp is\n  appended to the original name on a repeated deletion.\n- Add a new unrm xattr extension struct unrm_ts_append with\n  uta_orig_namelen, which is the length of the original name. With it\n  and URM_FL_TS_APPEND, the original name can be truncated out from\n  the renamed one in LinkEA.\n- Add llapi_fid2path_special/_at_special() to resolve both paths at\n  once. For a common object, the original path is its plain path and\n  the trash path is empty. For a trash can object, the original path\n  is the path it had before it was deleted, and the trash path is the\n  path it currently has in Trash Can.\n- Rebuild the original path on the client from the trash path: the\n  stub directory named after pFID is resolved by llapi_fid2path_at(),\n  and the original name of each deleted object is recovered by\n  truncating the name to uta_orig_namelen if URM_FL_TS_APPEND is set.\n- The \"trusted.unrm\" xattr is read through the virtual \".Trash\" of\n  the parent, so that the caller can have the same access to the\n  deleted objects.\n- Add \"--original|-o\" to \"lfs fid2path\" to print both paths in form\n  \"$orig_path -> $trash_path\". Without it, the live path is printed\n  for any FID as before.\n- Move the \"trusted.unrm\" helpers into lustreapi_internal.h so that\n  liblustreapi_trash.c and lfs.c can share them.\n- Add sanityn.sh test_117ze to verify this patch, which deletes a sub\n  directory with a file inside it repeatedly and checks both paths are\n  resolved correctly, and test_117zf to verify the same through a\n  subdir (FILESET) mount.\n- Add man pages llapi_fid2path.3 and llapi_fid2path_special.3, and\n  update lfs-fid2path.1 to reflect the new changes.\n\nLustre-change: https://review.whamcloud.com/69613\nLustre-commit: 7eadd19d470de5afcede9d2acd8da423951e505a\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=\"117,118,119\"\nSigned-off-by: Emoly Liu <emoly@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I16c799a18c6754a0cb477a40967d019be181530a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
